From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 16:25:32 +0200
Subject: MIPS: intel-mips: select HAVE_PCI and PCI_DRIVERS_GENERIC

The GRX350 carries three PCIe root complexes, and nothing in this
platform has ever been able to drive them, because INTEL_MIPS does not
select HAVE_PCI. CONFIG_PCI depends on it, so PCI cannot be turned on at
all here and every host controller driver is unreachable regardless of
what else the defconfig says.

Selecting HAVE_PCI alone is not enough, and the way it is not enough is
quiet. PCI_DRIVERS_LEGACY is "def_bool !PCI_DRIVERS_GENERIC", so a
platform that stays silent about which model it wants is handed the
legacy one: the arch keeps its own struct pci_controller, its own
pcibios_init(), and expects a driver to register a controller with it.
No modern host bridge driver does that. They all build a struct
pci_host_bridge and hand it to pci_host_probe(), which is what
PCI_DRIVERS_GENERIC arranges for. Picking the wrong half of that pair
does not produce a build error; it produces a bus that never gets
scanned.

PCI_DRIVERS_GENERIC also brings in PCI_DOMAINS_GENERIC ("select
PCI_DOMAINS_GENERIC if PCI"), which is what makes the "linux,pci-domain"
property in the root complex nodes mean anything. With three independent
root complexes on one SoC, each needing its own domain number, that is
not optional either.

Both go in the existing select list in its established order. This is
the same pair every other MIPS platform with a modern host bridge picks,
MACH_INGENIC and MIPS_GENERIC among them.

Deliberately not included is SWAP_IO_SPACE. Several MIPS platforms
select it alongside PCI, and it would look like it belongs here, but it
is not a PCI-scoped switch: it changes the byte order of readl() and
friends for the whole kernel image. This SoC's working GSWIP, CBM and
DMA ethernet datapath is written against the current, unswapped
accessors. The PCIe side pays for that decision instead, in the host
bridge driver, where the cost is contained.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/arch/mips/Kconfig b/arch/mips/Kconfig
index c1757c30a2aa..eddfc62918d9 100644
--- a/arch/mips/Kconfig
+++ b/arch/mips/Kconfig
@@ -488,11 +488,13 @@ config INTEL_MIPS
 	select CSRC_R4K
 	select DMA_NONCOHERENT
 	select GENERIC_ISA_DMA
+	select HAVE_PCI
 	select IRQ_MIPS_CPU
 	select MFD_CORE
 	select MFD_SYSCON
 	select MIPS_CPU_SCACHE
 	select MIPS_GIC
+	select PCI_DRIVERS_GENERIC
 	select SYS_HAS_CPU_MIPS32_R2
 	select SYS_HAS_CPU_MIPS32_R3_5
 	select SYS_SUPPORTS_BIG_ENDIAN
